From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: computerguy526 <355510486+computerguy526@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: persistent library cache (KK_LIBCACHE_DIR)

KK_LIBCACHE_DIR=<d> sets KK_METALLIB_DIR=<d>/lib (prebuilt metallibs, loaded
instead of compiling the MSL) and KK_MSL_COLLECT_DIR=<d>/msl (every MSL a
library is built from is written there) unless those variables are set
themselves. tools/kk-metallib/build_metallib.sh (scripts/kk-libcache-build.sh)
turns <d>/msl into <d>/lib offline, so a prepared cache loads its libraries in
0.3 ms instead of compiling them live.

Libraries are also deduplicated in memory by their key (KK_LIB_DEDUPE=0 turns
that off). The periodic pipeline-archive flush waits for the segment lock after
about a second of failed tries instead of skipping for ever, so eight builders
in flight no longer starve it (a prepare wrote 0 segments).

A pipeline archived from a source-compiled library never hits when the same
shader is later loaded from a metallib: prepare in two passes (nps5 cache
prepare does).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kosmickrisp/bridge/kk_libkey.h    |  37 ++++++++++
 src/kosmickrisp/bridge/mtl_compiler.m | 125 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 144 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/kk_libkey.h b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/kk_libkey.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e85f511
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/bridge/kk_libkey.h
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+/* Copyright nativeps5. SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+ *
+ * Content key of a Metal library built from MSL: SHA-256 over the build stamp
+ * (KosmicKrisp build + macOS build), the GPU name, the compile options and the
+ * MSL text, first 16 bytes as 32 hex digits. Kept separate (no Metal headers)
+ * so a unit test can include it. */
+#ifndef KK_LIBKEY_H
+#define KK_LIBKEY_H
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <CommonCrypto/CommonDigest.h>
+
+static inline void
+kk_libkey_compute(const char *stamp, const char *gpu, const char *src, int msl_version,
+                  int math_mode, int math_fp_fns, char out[33])
+{
+   CC_SHA256_CTX c;
+   unsigned char d[CC_SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH];
+   char opt[64];
+   CC_SHA256_Init(&c);
+   CC_SHA256_Update(&c, stamp, (CC_LONG)strlen(stamp));
+   CC_SHA256_Update(&c, gpu, (CC_LONG)strlen(gpu));
+   snprintf(opt, sizeof(opt), ";msl=%x;math=%d;fp=%d;", msl_version, math_mode, math_fp_fns);
+   CC_SHA256_Update(&c, opt, (CC_LONG)strlen(opt));
+   /* the text can exceed 4 GiB-safe CC_LONG only in theory; hash in chunks */
+   size_t n = strlen(src);
+   while (n) {
+      CC_LONG k = n > (1u << 30) ? (1u << 30) : (CC_LONG)n;
+      CC_SHA256_Update(&c, src, k);
+      src += k;
+      n -= k;
+   }
+   CC_SHA256_Final(d, &c);
+   for (int i = 0; i < 16; i++)
+      snprintf(out + i * 2, 3, "%02x", d[i]);
+}
+#endif
